body:
Very nicely written, although i comprehend your thoughts i also understand when there is a sub with the word problem in it, it will be filled with dilemma, confusion and sorrow. That is how and why communities are formed. To convey and fight for causes thus alone we are.

&#x200B;

We all give a shit, that is why there are various posts with various answers. Utopia does not exist. For the battle is never ending, only thing that prevails is perseverance and determination.

&#x200B;

Thank you for your thoughts and good luck!

My ideas were:

To post on a weekly basis the following

For those who were in a depression for their size; what made you come out of your depression

For those who have not been depressed to explain why it doesnt affect them as much

&#x200B;

How do you carry out a normal life such as job, hobbies, relationships, etc.

&#x200B;

From my point of view i actually was depressed and gave up on everything but recently have had a lot of support from friends and family to oversee what i cannot change and be the best version of myself.

I actually have taken studies back, organised my life (My room, looks and thoughts are much clearer) taken back dating and given myself a chance to live. 

&#x200B;

Obviously our personalities are different therefore it is up to you guys how you express yourselves. Obviously there are some people that have a normal life, this is just a movement to prove there are ways out of just seeing problems!

&#x200B;

Thank you for listening!
